From: custom_rv32
Subject: [PATCH] cache model: stats at any exit, trace marker gating

Spike prints the --ic/--dc/--l2 statistics from the cache destructors,
which only run when main() returns. The "quit" debug command and a
second Ctrl-c call exit() instead, so the statistics were lost. Print
them from atexit() too (once), and to the file named by
SPIKE_CACHE_STATS if it's set.

With SPIKE_TRACE_GATE set, only count accesses between the trace markers
"addi x0, x0, 0x5a1" (on) and "addi x0, x0, 0x5a0" (off), the same
markers that gate --log-commits. The markers are detected in addi
itself, so this works without --log-commits. Outside the window the
cache contents are still simulated, so each window starts warm. The
instructions retired inside the windows are reported too, with misses
per 1K instructions for each cache.

Also report a 0% miss rate instead of NaN for a cache with no accesses.

See docs/tracing.md in the custom_rv32 external tree.
---
--- a/riscv/cachesim.cc
+++ b/riscv/cachesim.cc
@@ -5,11 +5,71 @@
 #include <cstdlib>
 #include <iostream>
 #include <iomanip>
+#include <fstream>
+#include <vector>
+#include <algorithm>
+
+static const bool gate = getenv("SPIKE_TRACE_GATE") != nullptr;
+bool cache_sim_t::counting = !gate;
+
+// Instructions retired inside trace windows
+static uint64_t window_insns = 0;
+static uint64_t window_start = 0;
+
+static std::vector<cache_sim_t*>& all_caches()
+{
+  static std::vector<cache_sim_t*> caches;
+  return caches;
+}
+
+// Spike's "quit" command and a second Ctrl-c call exit(), which skips the
+// destructors in main(), so the statistics are printed from atexit() too.
+static void register_cache(cache_sim_t* c)
+{
+  if (all_caches().empty())
+    std::atexit(cache_sim_t::print_all_stats);
+  all_caches().push_back(c);
+}
+
+void cache_sim_t::trace_marker(bool on, uint64_t minstret)
+{
+  if (!gate || on == counting)
+    return;
+  counting = on;
+  if (on)
+    window_start = minstret;
+  else
+    window_insns += minstret - window_start;
+}
+
+void cache_sim_t::print_all_stats()
+{
+  static bool printed = false;
+  if (printed || all_caches().empty())
+    return;
+  printed = true;
+
+  const char* path = getenv("SPIKE_CACHE_STATS");
+  std::ofstream file;
+  if (path) {
+    file.open(path);
+    if (!file)
+      std::cerr << "spike: can't write cache statistics to " << path << std::endl;
+  }
+  std::ostream& out = file.is_open() ? file : std::cout;
+
+  // A window still open at exit is counted up to its last marker only
+  if (gate)
+    out << "Window Instructions:      " << window_insns << std::endl;
+  for (auto c : all_caches())
+    c->print_stats(out);
+}
 
 cache_sim_t::cache_sim_t(size_t _sets, size_t _ways, size_t _linesz, const char* _name)
 : sets(_sets), ways(_ways), linesz(_linesz), name(_name), log(false)
 {
   init();
+  register_cache(this);
 }
 
